    text: "Everyday clothing is what most people wear for daily activities — work, errands, and casual outings. The basics include a T-shirt, which is the most universal garment, worn by people of all ages. Jeans are equally popular — durable, comfortable, and suitable for almost any informal occasion. A hoodie or sweatshirt provides warmth on cool days, while a jacket or coat is essential in colder weather. For the upper body, options range from a simple blouse or shirt to a cardigan or pullover. Trousers come in many styles: chinos, leggings, joggers, and cargo pants each serve different purposes. Shorts are common in warm weather, and a skirt or dress offers alternatives for those who prefer them. Underwear — including briefs, boxers, socks, and undershirts — forms the invisible foundation of every outfit. Sleepwear like pyjamas and a dressing gown keeps you comfortable at home. Seasonal items like a raincoat, scarf, gloves, and a beanie or woolly hat protect against the elements. Understanding everyday clothing vocabulary helps with shopping, packing for trips, and describing what people are wearing — a skill tested in every language exam.",
